    "body": "## Motivation\nThe reason for this PR is to resolve a future or the needs of using non pinned transformers.\nfrom current pinned 5.5.3,!=5.6.0,<5.13\n\n## What is wrong\n\n`qwen3_5_decoder_layer_forward` (the patched `Qwen3_5DecoderLayer.forward`) reads `self.layer_type`.\ntransformers 5.13.0 renamed that decoder-layer attribute to `block_type`, so on transformers >= 5.13 the first\nforward raises:\n\n    AttributeError: 'FSDPQwen3_5DecoderLayer' object has no attribute 'layer_type'\n\n(The `FSDP...` prefix is just FSDP2's dynamic subclass of the layer; the attribute is missing on the layer itself.)\n\nWhich transformers versions have which name (checked from the wheels' `modeling_qwen3_5.py`):\n\n| transformers | `Qwen3_5DecoderLayer` attribute |\n|---|---|\n| 5.10.4, 5.11.0, 5.12.0 | `layer_type` |\n| 5.13.0 - 5.17.0 | `block_type` |\n\n## Fix\n\nRead the name that exists: `getattr(self, \"layer_type\", None) or self.block_type`. Works on both sides of the rename,\nso the pin can move later without another change.\n\n## Test\n\nNew CPU-only unit test `tests/models/test_qwen3_5_decoder_layer_forward.py` (tiny random full-attention layer).\n\n| transformers | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| 5.12.1 | pass | pass |\n| 5.17.0 | FAIL (AttributeError above) | pass |",
    "changed_files": 2,
