      "body": "<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n<a href=\"https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/verl-project/verl/pull/8255?scope=ghh_OusAJGA4HG8ljoOV0wJvVx8NmnZIjc2DdjmxOu0xZWA&amp;cs_source=review_comment\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui-dark.svg?v=3\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg?v=3\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg?v=3\" alt=\"Review in Change Stack →\" height=\"32\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>📝 Summary</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved compatibility with Qwen3.5 models that use either supported decoder-layer attribute name to select the attention type.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\nThe Qwen3.5 decoder forward function now reads the layer type from `layer_type` or, if unavailable, `block_type`. A parameterized CPU test checks the forward output shape for both attribute names.\n\n**Changes: Qwen3.5 decoder layer compatibility**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|:---|:---|\n|**Layer-type fallback and forward test** <br> `verl/models/transformers/qwen3_5.py`, `tests/models/test_qwen3_5_decoder_layer_forward_on_cpu.py`|The decoder forward function falls back to `block_type` when `layer_type` is unavailable. The CPU test checks that both attribute names produce an output with the input shape.|\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- change_assessment_start -->\n**Priority:** ➖ Normal\n\n<!-- change_assessment_commit:\"9b7d3e3cb5709e48d292145f859a77cdcd9c945b\" -->\n\n<!-- change_assessment_end -->\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Merge Risk:</strong> <strong>⚪ Minimal</strong> · up to <code>9b7d3</code></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<!-- final_review_risk_start -->\n<!-- final_review_risk_label\n**Merge Risk:** **⚪ Minimal** · up to `9b7d3`\n-->\n<!-- final_review_risk_coverage:{\"sourceCommitId\":\"9b7d3e3cb5709e48d292145f859a77cdcd9c945b\",\"coveredCommitId\":\"9b7d3e3cb5709e48d292145f859a77cdcd9c945b\",\"kind\":\"reviewed\"} -->\n\nThe decoder supports both attribute names, but the new CPU test covers only full-attention dispatch. Adding linear-attention coverage is a narrow improvement; no merge-blocking runtime risk is established.\n<!-- final_review_risk_end -->\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Pre-merge checks: <sup><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-counter-passed-14-v2.svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" align=\"middle\" alt=\"Passed\" title=\"Passed\"></picture></sup> 4 · <sup><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-counter-failed-14-v2.svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" align=\"middle\" alt=\"Failed\" title=\"Failed\"></picture></sup> 1</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<strong><sup><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-counter-failed-14-v2.svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" align=\"middle\" alt=\"Failed\" title=\"Failed\"></picture></sup> Failed checks: 1 warning</strong>\n\n|     Check name     |                                              Status                                              | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                               | Resolution                                                         